        "prompt": "You assess the shape of a software engineering request.\n\nA request is ARCHITECTURE when it asks for system or API design, a multi-file or multi-service refactor, a migration plan, a performance or concurrency investigation across components, a security review, or a trade-off analysis between approaches.\n\nA request is ROUTINE when it asks about syntax, a single function or small snippet, the meaning of an error message, a regular expression, a shell one-liner, a library's basic usage, or a quick explanation of a concept.",
        "labels": [
          "ARCHITECTURE",
          "ROUTINE"
        ],
        "default_label": "ROUTINE",
        "on_error": "match_false"
      }
    ],
    "rules": [
